                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>This statement was incorrect.&nbsp;Bismuth subsalicylate is a medication that directly soothes the GIT, and as such is not considered an antiemetic. It may soothe some of the discomfort due to its direct anti-inflammatory effects and the decrease in stomach acids which may be contributing to the problem.&nbsp;</div>\n",
